# Acutis verification core

Acutis verifies AI-generated code before it enters the codebase. Call the verify_code tool with the exact code you are about to write and a PCST contract, and write only text that received ALLOW. A pre-write gate denies any code-file write that lacks an ALLOW covering the exact text.

Rules that make the first call ALLOW:
1. Write code files (.py .js .jsx .ts .tsx .mjs .cjs .java) with the Write or Edit tools, never through shell redirection, heredocs, sed, or scripts. Bash is for running things. If a command (formatter, generator) rewrites a code file, verify that file's final text afterwards.
2. Submit a parseable unit (whole function, class, or file), not an indented fragment. Use language python, javascript, typescript, tsx, or java.
3. Identify sources (request params, body fields, route params, CLI args, env values, file names, external JSON) and declare them. Function parameters are user-controlled even when undeclared.
4. Enumerate EVERY call site before the first call, named as the parser names them: dotted member chains as written without parentheses (db.select.where, res.status.json, new Hono().post); bare helpers and builders (eq, z.object) are calls; JSX attributes and spreads are call sites named by the attribute (value, onClick, key, className; {...props} is props); template tags are calls.
5. Classify each name once: a boundary sink with its category, a transform with its effect (real sanitizer or validator calls only), or SafeOutput for everything else. With no declared sources every parsed call must be declared. A name is a sink OR a transform, never both. Never submit an empty or partial contract to discover the list.
6. Valid categories, the only accepted names: HTMLOutput, SQLQuery, JSONOutput, URLSink, SafeOutput, CommandExecution, FileSystemPath, OutboundHTTPRequest, NetworkTransmission, CodeEvaluation, UnsafeDeserialization, HTTPRedirect, HTTPHeader, LogOutput, LDAPQuery, XPathQuery, NoSQLQuery, CSVCell, DynamicImport, Reflection, SignedPayloadUse, FormatString, TemplateRenderer, XMLDOMBuilder, ArgvExec.
7. On BLOCK_INCOMPLETE declare every name in missing_coverage in one revision; on BLOCK_VIOLATION fix the code, never weaken a category. Omit witnesses.
8. Write the verified text byte-for-byte; verify the final version, not a draft.

Contract shape: {"sources": ["request.args.get"], "sinks": [{"name": "render_html", "category": "HTMLOutput"}], "transforms": [{"name": "escape_html", "effect": "EscapesHTML"}]}

For examples, multi-argument sinks, arg roles, policy attributes, and BLOCK troubleshooting, load the verify skill (/acutis:verify) and its references.

In Cursor, write code files with the Write tool.
